# mv/deps.list
#
# Shared-library dependencies per design/tooling/plan.md §6.3 + §7.
# Each line names one library, its minimum required semver, and the
# mv module(s) that link it. The `pkg install mv` resolver enforces
# the semver constraints before staging the mv package tree under
# /pkgs/mv-1.0.0/; a mismatch (missing or too-old library) is an
# install-time exit 5 (signing/verification failure -- the manifest
# no longer verifies against the installed substrate).
#
# Format: <name> <min-semver>  # <mv module(s)>
#
# Order matches src/ file order (mv, argv, rename, move, inode,
# schema, audit, undo, elevate, verbose, pdxfs) so a reviewer can
# cross-check module-level dependencies against link-list entries.
#
# mv.ENH-008 (paideia-os/mv#24): this list originally named five
# libraries but only one (libpdx-argv) was ever actually called --
# src/mv.pdx + src/inode.pdx, src/schema.pdx, and src/elevate.pdx all
# use LOCAL trampolines against the raw R20b/PdxFS syscalls instead of
# libpdx-cap / libpdx-semantic-pipe / libpdx-elevate, so those three
# entries were spurious install-time failure modes (`pkg install mv`
# enforces every entry's semver constraint). libpdx-audit is now also
# real: src/audit.pdx calls its AuditClient (audit_begin /
# audit_record_output / audit_commit) instead of hand-rolling raw IPC
# against svc.audit-journal in a shape AuditBroker did not agree with.
# The other three entries are removed rather than kept-and-noted: an
# installer-enforced dependency the source never calls is a defect,
# not documentation debt. Re-add libpdx-cap / libpdx-semantic-pipe /
# libpdx-elevate here in the SAME commit that wires src/mv.pdx+src/
# inode.pdx, src/schema.pdx, or src/elevate.pdx to the real crate.

libpdx-argv            1.0.0   # argv surface + flag parse; src/argv.pdx
libpdx-audit           1.0.0   # user-events journal client (AuditClient); src/audit.pdx
